Query: Read /workspace/autoresearch/README.md, /workspace/autoresearch/program.md, /workspace/autoresearch/context.md, and /workspace/autoresearch/AGENTS.md first. 
Then read ${SGLANG_REPO}/context.txt and ${SGLANG_REPO}/marconi.txt if they exist.

You are using /workspace/autoresearch only as the evaluation harness and experiment log. The code to improve is in /workspace/sglang on branch marconi-eviction or its 
current clean worktree equivalent. Do not commit.

Environment and operating assumptions for this batch:
- workspace: /workspace/autoresearch
- target repo: /workspace/sglang
- target branch: marconi-eviction
- hardware proxy: 1xH100
- model: nvidia/NVIDIA-Nemotron-Nano-9B-v2
- tensor parallel size: 1
- eval mode: fast
- context length: 32768
- public API must stay aligned with --radix-eviction-policy marconi
- for this Nemotron setup, use MARCONI_EXTRA_SERVER_ARGS='--mamba-scheduler-strategy no_buffer' when running train.py

At the very start of the batch, explicitly rebuild continuity before changing anything:
1. cd /workspace/autoresearch
2. ensure these env vars are set for this run:
   - SGLANG_REPO=/workspace/sglang
   - MARCONI_MODEL_PATH=nvidia/NVIDIA-Nemotron-Nano-9B-v2
   - MARCONI_TP_SIZE=1
   - MARCONI_MIN_GPUS=1
   - MARCONI_EVAL_MODE=fast
   - MARCONI_CONTEXT_LENGTH=32768
   - MARCONI_RESULTS_DIR=/workspace/autoresearch/results
   - MARCONI_EXTRA_SERVER_ARGS=--mamba-scheduler-strategy no_buffer
3. read /workspace/autoresearch/results.tsv
4. read /workspace/autoresearch/baselines.tsv if it exists
5. inspect git branch, commit, and diff state in /workspace/sglang
6. read /workspace/autoresearch/context.md again
7. continue from the best current local repo state you find rather than starting from scratch

This batch is bounded. Do exactly 3 research iterations, no more and no less.

Important shift in strategy:
- Be aggressive and high-upside.
- Stop spending most iterations on tiny weight-grid or tiny threshold tweaks.
- Treat Marconi autotuning as an online controller problem, not just “pick the best weight from a small grid on the last window.”
- Prefer changes that improve what the tuner sees, what it optimizes, or how it decides, rather than just where it samples.
- Stay on marconi-eviction, not marconi-admission, unless strong evidence shows admission is the bottleneck.

Moonshot priority tracks, in order:
1. pressure-aware replay-window redesign
   - redesign which requests enter the tuning window so the tuner learns from pressure-bearing, replay-informative requests
   - prefer segments near real eviction pressure, insert-heavy periods, replay-heavy periods, queue buildup, or occupancy stress rather than naive recent history
   - if feasible with small-to-medium code changes, build or approximate an event-aware / segment-aware tuning window instead of a plain rolling tail
   - this is the highest-priority track
2. robust objective redesign
   - stop relying purely on raw winner-take-all replay score
   - prefer objectives that reward stable marginal improvement over the current weight and robust local optima
   - consider neighborhood support, local score floor, repeated evidence, or confidence-style penalties for noisy winner spikes
   - do not smuggle in a hidden favorite eff_weight
3. staged controller / multi-phase tuner redesign
   - explicitly separate discovery, validation, and refinement behavior
   - use different policies for first-round exploration vs later steady-state tuning
   - consider validation passes, evidence budgets, hysteresis, or repeat-confirmation before switching away from a good active weight
4. uncertainty handling only as part of a deeper design
   - weak-surface freeze, skip, or caution logic is allowed only when integrated into one of the moonshot tracks above, not as an isolated micro-threshold tweak

Exploration policy:
- In each batch, at least 2 of the 3 iterations must target one of the first 3 moonshot tracks above.
- Do not spend two consecutive iterations on the same tiny grid-shape or threshold variant unless the prior run clearly improved.
- After any 2 consecutive regressions in one theme, switch to a different moonshot track.
- Micro-grid tuning is only allowed when it is clearly supporting one of the moonshot tracks above.
- Prefer one small-to-medium conceptual redesign over several tiny reactive patches.

Recommended batch pattern:
- one iteration on pressure-aware / event-aware replay-window construction
- one iteration on robust objective redesign
- one iteration on staged controller / validation / hysteresis behavior
If a clear win appears in one track, the next batch may continue that track once before rotating.

For each of the 3 iterations:
1. inspect current target repo branch/commit/dirty state
2. choose one hypothesis from the moonshot tracks above
3. make one small-to-medium code-level change in /workspace/sglang only
4. run exactly one experiment from /workspace/autoresearch with:
   uv run --no-sync train.py > run.log 2>&1
5. read the summary from /workspace/autoresearch/run.log
6. append a row to /workspace/autoresearch/results.tsv
7. keep the local target-repo change only if it improves autotune-enabled throughput for this proxy setup; otherwise revert just your last change
8. do not commit

Constraints:
- do not mainly edit the harness unless it is clearly broken
- do not broaden into unrelated Marconi work
- do not change benchmark methodology in a way that breaks comparability
- do not hardcode a hidden favorite eff_weight fallback
- keep the public user contract aligned with --radix-eviction-policy marconi
- scheduled run must stay bounded to 3 iterations

Primary objective:
- improve autotune-enabled request throughput
- and, when a main-branch non-Marconi baseline is available in /workspace/autoresearch/baselines.tsv, beat that reference on throughput and TTFT

Secondary objective:
- lower mean TTFT

At the end of this batch, produce a concise summary containing exactly:
- iterations completed
- best throughput seen this run
- best mean TTFT seen this run
- whether any local change is worth keeping
- current target branch and commit
- delivery note that results.tsv was updated in /workspace/autoresearch
